indeed it was for us a very  important historical moment first of all  to make sure that  the european union stands firmly at the  side  of india in this most challenging time  and we assure the prime minister of our  solidarity  and the support um with all what is  needed at the moment being from  ex-oxygen generators  to medicines and ventilators  it was a remarkable summit because  it widened the scope and the view  on the untapped potential in the  relationship of the european union  and india and we have agreed that we  will resume  the negotiations on a free trade  agreement  we will also launch negotiations on  investment  production protection and of  negotiations on the important topic of  geographical  indications we also discussed the topic  of climate change  india is the fourth biggest emitter of  greenhouse gases in the world  and it is impressive to see  how india is stepping forward now in  this topic  too we discussed the  importance of committing to climate  neutrality  and complete phase out from fossil fuels  for example in view of the crucial  un cop 26 6 and last but not least  our partnership on connectivity it is  the second  only of such a connectivity partnership  after japan it will bring our two  regions closer  in mobility and transport but of course  also  in the digital field india is a  powerhouse of digitization  so this shows the width and these were  only a few examples  of the cooperation with india thanks  again to antonio costa for having  convened this summit  thank you
 

